# BMAD Agent Architecture

## Module Responsibilities

| Module | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `extension.ts` | Activation, chat participant registration, command wiring |
| `bmadResources.ts` | Phase definitions (questions, deliverables, checklists) |
| `copilotBridge.ts` | Prompt construction and Copilot LLM delegation |
| `lmStudioClient.ts` | HTTP client for LM Studio (OpenAI-compatible) |
| `lmChatContext.ts` | Persistent LM Studio conversation storage |
| `lmChatViewProvider.ts` | Webview provider for LM Studio Chat panel |
| `sidebarProvider.ts` | Webview provider for BMAD Control Panel |
| `scaffolding.ts` | Workspace artifact generation (plan, context, tasks, IDE configs) |
| `accessControl.ts` | Access mode types (read / workspace / full) |
| `modelSelection.ts` | Model configuration and selection logic |
| `resourceLoader.ts` | JSON resource file loading from dist/ |
| `storageKeys.ts` | Centralised workspace/global state key constants |
| `taskQueue.ts` | In-memory + persisted task queue for LM Studio tool calls |

## Data Flow

```
User answers (4 phases) → CollectedAnswers
  → copilotBridge.buildPrompt() → Copilot LLM
  → lmStudioClient.sendChat() → LM Studio
  → scaffolding.generateBmAdScaffolding() → workspace files
```

## Extension Points

- Chat participants are registered via `contributes.chatParticipants` in `package.json`.
- Webview providers implement `vscode.WebviewViewProvider`.
- Commands are registered in `activate()` and declared in `contributes.commands`.

## Important Patterns

- Conversations are tracked via a `WeakMap<vscode.ChatContext, string>` for memory efficiency.
- The Copilot bridge maintains an LRU model cache (max 5 per conversation).
- LM Studio requests include `just_in_time: true` for on-demand context rehydration.
- Resources are copied from `src/resources/` to `dist/resources/` during build.
